y month by month, and we base that on done strategies on the situation actually.</p><p>Bob Duncan: Yes, We based it on this, which is what we have done as a business.</p><p>Bob Duncan: And by month, by quarter, How many apps we&#x27;re doing just to make sure that we know effectively we&#x27;re looking at twenty six percent of our business in Q. One, twenty seven percent in Q two, twenty percent in Q three and twenty seven percent on Q four. That is the you.</p><p>Speaker 3: Know it&#x27;s not a big change.</p><p>Bob Duncan: That is how your numbers will play out for the year. So you will know Q one you are going to be pretty busy. Q two busier. March on Q three is going to be quiet, Q four is going to be really busy. Yeah, But then that number bear in mind will change as we continue to grow the business because we will start to get renewals coming through, in November and December and October, meaning that the likelihood is with migration business and the quiet months. Yeah.</p><p>Bob Duncan: And what I mean by that, just so it doesn&#x27;t sound like I am just talking gibberish, um, but I think we had Karen&#x27;s up there. There on if you go to Karen for twenty six twenty seven, She&#x27;s got fifteen cases that she will write in December because all that she can&#x27;t remortgage them now unless the lenders allow us to do six months out. She&#x27;s going to do one in December. Yeah, and you will be the same at some point. You will get to a point where you&#x27;ve got this tranche of cases, you&#x27;ll end up doing quite a month, which is good because then you&#x27;ll end up hopefully with a belt. Yeah,</p><p>Craig Roberts: That was always in Melbough Jerry and Alan Hardest. Do you know Jerry McCrea? He said your home script. Yeah, yeah. Jerry always said December&#x27;s our busy month; it&#x27;s remortgage month because you&#x27;ll have no appointments;. That&#x27;s the month. We do all your remortgages, then. And you&#x27;ll have a busier month than you would normally think because Julie remarked just in December. You can see that Karen has,</p><p>Bob Duncan: Yeah, It just takes a bit of time, and it&#x27;s you know because you can&#x27;t change when we&#x27;re entitled. Yeah, your mortgage is up, you&#x27;ve got to do it. I mean, you could January but the reality is are you going to get in January? You know but anyway I think we will get there. I think with what you&#x27;ve committed there. I&#x27;m I feel quite confident and getting there. Number of things that we need to work on, but we&#x27;ll put them into our action plans for next year. So I&#x27;ve got end of year meetings, I need to put them in. We&#x27;re done before the end of this month. Topic for them in for next week, And then that will just be the kind of backbone to how we&#x27;re going to get to target. So what&#x27;s the specific effects for you that we&#x27;re going to focus on? But then what does that.</p><p>Bob Duncan: Actually, look like throughout the year, you know. So rather than we want to get to ninety applications, right? Well, how are we going to do that? What are we going to focus on to make sure we get that? Yeah. Mhm. Yep. Okay. Perfect. Anything you want to ask Aden? Are you feeling quite comfortable hitting two cases a week? It doesn&#x27;t sound like a big number when you say that.</p><p>Craig Roberts: No doesn&#x27;t does it if he&#x27;s even when you start to multiply out, you&#x27;re like three, four, six, one a week, and that&#x27;s quite a lot, but it&#x27;s two cases. It&#x27;s not so bad. And if you can get that bouncing ball of doing your mortgage and doing your protection. Yep, it might not be the same people, but it&#x27;s the same. But if you can get protection and mortgages, and it&#x27;s one week behind almost, then it&#x27;s fine. Yeah, as long as it&#x27;s consistent.</p><p>Bob Duncan: It&#x27;s a consistency piece; you&#x27;ll always find quiet times. But as you start to grow your back book, The quiet times will become essentially mortgages at one because they will naturally fall under that window. And you&#x27;ll have a better month of mortgages. Yeah yeah Cool right perfect I will get that all finished, Um and then once it&#x27;s all done, I&#x27;ll share everyone&#x27;s individual plans with them. Um and then that lays the foundation next year for everyone. All right, perfect. All right, magic. All right, thank you. See you soon.</p></body></html>